<section class="best-worlds-stage" aria-labelledby="best-worlds-heading" aria-describedby="best-worlds-description">
  <h2 id="best-worlds-heading" class="sr-only">
    The flexibility of model reasoning and the consistency of formal program analysis combined
  </h2>
  <p id="best-worlds-description" class="sr-only">
    OpenTaint discovers application-specific vulnerability patterns, turns them into readable formal specifications, and enforces them with repeatable whole-project analysis on every code change.
  </p>

  <div class="best-worlds-inner">
    <div class="best-worlds-visual">
      <svg class="best-worlds-flow" viewBox="0 0 1200 560" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <path class="best-worlds-flow-muted" d="M374 294 H434 M766 294 H826" />
        <path class="best-worlds-flow-active" d="M374 294 H434 M766 294 H826" />
      </svg>

      <article class="best-worlds-side best-worlds-reasoning">
        <header class="best-worlds-side-heading">
          <small>AGENTIC / DISCOVER</small>
          <h3>The flexibility of <strong>model reasoning</strong></h3>
        </header>

        <p class="best-worlds-outcome best-worlds-reasoning-outcome">
          Adapts security knowledge to your application
        </p>

        <div class="best-worlds-values" aria-label="Values of model reasoning">
          <div>
            <span class="best-worlds-value-symbol" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M5 9a7 7 0 0 1 14 0v2M8 10a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3M12 10v7M7 14c0 3 1 5 3 7M17 15c0 2-.5 4-1.5 6" /></svg>
            </span>
            <span><b>FINDS NEW VULNERABILITY PATTERNS</b><small>Identifies dangerous behavior that was not defined before the review.</small></span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="best-worlds-value-symbol" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M8 4H4v4M16 4h4v4M20 16v4h-4M8 20H4v-4" /><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3" /></svg>
            </span>
            <span><b>UNDERSTANDS APPLICATION CONTEXT</b><small>Uses architecture, trust boundaries, and intended behavior to assess a finding.</small></span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="best-worlds-value-symbol" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><rect x="3.5" y="4" width="6" height="5" rx="1" /><rect x="14.5" y="4" width="6" height="5" rx="1" /><rect x="9" y="15" width="6" height="5" rx="1" /><path d="M6.5 9v2.5H17.5V9M12 11.5V15" /></svg>
            </span>
            <span><b>UNDERSTANDS CODE DEPENDENCIES</b><small>Uses knowledge of frameworks, libraries, and APIs to explain security behavior.</small></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="best-worlds-core">
        <header>
          <span>LEAN / SPECIFY</span>
          <strong>CODE TO FORMAL SPECIFICATION</strong>
        </header>

        <div class="best-worlds-code-map">
          <section class="best-worlds-code-panel best-worlds-application-code" aria-label="Spring application code with the taint source, transformation, and sink highlighted">
            <header><span>SPRING APPLICATION CODE</span><i>PreviewController.java</i></header>
            <pre><code><span>@PostMapping("/preview")</span>
<span class="code-line-source">String <b class="code-object-method">preview</b>(PreviewDto <b class="code-object-source">dto</b>) &#123;</span>
<span class="code-line-transform">  var <b class="code-object-data">view</b> = dto.template().strip();</span>
<span class="code-line-soft">  audit("preview_requested");</span>
<span class="code-line-sink">  return <b class="code-object-sink">engine</b>.process(<b class="code-object-data">view</b>,</span>
<span class="code-line-sink">      context);</span>
<span>&#125;</span></code></pre>
          </section>

          <div class="best-worlds-bindings" aria-label="Metavariables bound to objects in the application code">
            <strong>METAVARIABLES ARE DATA TAINT MARKS</strong>
            <div>
              <code><b class="code-meta-method">$METHOD</b> = <span class="code-object-method">preview</span></code>
              <code><b class="code-meta-source">$SOURCE</b> = <span class="code-object-source">dto</span></code>
              <code><b class="code-meta-source">$DATA</b> = <span class="code-object-data">view</span></code>
              <code><b class="code-meta-sink">$ENGINE</b> = <span class="code-object-sink">engine</span></code>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="best-worlds-dependency-model" aria-label="Dependency model propagating taint through String strip">
            <strong>DEPENDENCY MODEL</strong>
            <code>String#strip &#123; result = this; &#125;</code>
          </div>

          <section class="best-worlds-code-panel best-worlds-formal-code" aria-label="Formal SSTI specification expressed with metavariables">
            <header><span>FORMAL SPECIFICATION</span><i>Java pattern</i></header>
            <pre><code><span><b class="code-meta-data">$RETURN</b> <b class="code-meta-method">$METHOD</b>(...,</span>
<span>  PreviewDto <b class="code-meta-source">$SOURCE</b>, ...) &#123;</span>
<span class="code-line-ellipsis">  ...</span>
<span>  <b class="code-meta-sink">$ENGINE</b>.process(<b class="code-meta-source">$DATA</b>, ...);</span>
<span>&#125;</span></code></pre>
          </section>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="best-worlds-side best-worlds-analysis">
        <header class="best-worlds-side-heading">
          <small>CONTINUOUS / SCAN</small>
          <h3>The consistency of <strong>formal program analysis</strong></h3>
        </header>

        <p class="best-worlds-outcome best-worlds-analysis-outcome">
          Finds every match for each security rule
        </p>

